<!--
  Story 2.3 — leading icon for the regional-bias note in DetailPanelContent
  (UX-DR8 content order; UX spec § Component Strategy AnchoredDetailPanel).

  Drawn inline as a VectorDrawable rather than pulled from
  androidx.compose.material:material-icons-extended (+1.5 MB APK delta,
  violating NFR2 < 10 MB budget). The path data is the public Material
  Symbol "public" 24 dp filled glyph (Apache-2.0). DetailPanelContent
  ships it at 16 dp via the bias-row Icon() composable.

  fillColor is bound to @color/vs_on_background_muted (defined in
  res/values/colors.xml + res/values-night/colors.xml) — the project's
  own muted-text token already used for "context, regional-bias note"
  per UX Step 8. Auto-switches light/dark via the platform configuration
  qualifiers. The Compose Icon() composable still applies its own tint
  at the call site, taking precedence over the drawable's intrinsic fill.

  Spec AC #8 mandated `?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant`, but that attribute
  is not defined in the project's theme stack (the V1 theme parent is
  `android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar`, not a Material3 Components
  Views theme). The semantic intent — theme-aware muted icon colour —
  is preserved via the project token. Spec-author follow-up tracked in
  deferred-work.md.
-->
